IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 267 (piece dg8, lines 1372 to 1380):
-- merger of parent entity and subsidiary corporation or corporations (the "short-form" merger into or out of a 90 percent owner that is an entity).
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online, made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- Quote lines below are slices of that file: `-- src:N | ...` is line N, and an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation that is, or may become, the subsidiary: a minority stockholder asking
-- whether the parent may merge the corporation away without their vote, whether they have appraisal rights, and whether the terms can make them a general
-- partner; a director asking what the parent must file. The seat layer dg8-seat.l4 asks these rules from that side.
--
-- Section 114(b)(2) takes section 267 out of the reading of "stockholder" as "member" (and "stock" as "membership interest") for a nonstock corporation:
-- section 267 speaks of shares of stock and stockholders only, and is read as written.
--
-- What the section leaves to law outside this module is an input, named for the fact with its section, and listed in NOTES.md:
--   * the provision a certificate of incorporation must contain under section 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) (piece dg6), which takes a corporation out of the 90 percent test;
--   * section 103 (piece dg1) for acknowledging and filing; section 252(d) (piece dg6) for service of process upon a foreign survivor;
--   * sections 259, 260, 261, 328 (pieces dg7, dg10) and 251(e) (piece dg6), applied by reference; section 262 (piece dg7), to which subsection (c) points;
--   * the entity's governing documents and the law of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized: not among the inputs.

§ `s 267(d) The terms the section defines for itself`

-- "As used in this section only": "entity" means a partnership (of the four kinds), limited liability company, any association of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or
-- joint-stock company and any unincorporated association, trust or enterprise having members or having outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest, whether formed under
-- the laws of this State or any other jurisdiction. A predicate over the core `Kind of entity` (keel instruction 12). A corporation is not an "entity" here (the section keeps "entity" and "corporation" apart);
-- a natural person is not either. For a trust, an association or an enterprise that is not a partnership, a limited liability company or a joint-stock association, the definition turns on a fact about it
-- (members, shares or other evidences of interest), taken as a plain input (fork F16).
-- src:1378 | (2) “Entity” means a partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), limited liability company, any association of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or joint-stock company and any unincorporated association, trust or enterprise having members or having outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest therein, whether formed or organized by agreement or under statutory authority or otherwise and whether formed or organized under the laws of this State or the laws of any other jurisdiction; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(d)(2) (src:1378)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of entity`
      `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(d)(2) the term entity` MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a general partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a limited liability company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a joint-stock association` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory trust` THEN `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `a business trust or association` THEN `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `a real estate investment trust` THEN `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `a common-law trust` THEN `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `any other unincorporated business or association` THEN `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "Constituent party": an entity or corporation to be merged pursuant to the section.
-- src:1377 | (1) “Constituent party” means an entity or corporation to be merged pursuant to this section;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(d)(1) (src:1377)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of entity`
      `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be merged pursuant to the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(d)(1) the term constituent party` MEANS
        (   `s 267(d)(2) the term entity` k `it has members or outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
         OR CONSIDER k
            WHEN `a corporation` kk THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `it is to be merged pursuant to the section`

-- "Governing documents": a partnership agreement, limited liability company agreement, articles of association or any other instrument containing the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized.
-- src:1379 | (3) “Governing documents” means a partnership agreement, limited liability company agreement, articles of association or any other instrument containing the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(d)(3) (src:1379)
DECLARE `s 267(d)(3) Instrument` IS ONE OF
    `a partnership agreement under s 267(d)(3)`
    `a limited liability company agreement under s 267(d)(3)`
    `articles of association under s 267(d)(3)`
    `any other instrument containing the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized under s 267(d)(3)`
    `an instrument that does not contain the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized under s 267(d)(3)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(d)(3) (src:1379)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 267(d)(3) Instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(d)(3) the term governing documents` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `an instrument that does not contain the provisions by which an entity is formed or organized under s 267(d)(3)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `s 267(a) When the entity may merge the corporation or corporations into itself, or itself into one of them`

-- (a)(1): "at least 90% of the outstanding shares of each class of the stock of a corporation or corporations (other than a corporation which has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required
-- by § 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)), of which class there are outstanding shares that, absent this subsection, would be entitled to vote on such merger, is owned by an entity". One record per class; the test is
-- "at least": reaching 90% is enough (core fork F4). A class that does not count (no outstanding shares that would be entitled to vote, or its corporation has the section 251(g)(7) provision) is left out.
-- If no class counts, the test has nothing to measure and answers NOTHING; so do counts that cannot be a holding.
-- src:1373 | (a) In any case in which: (1) at least 90% of the outstanding shares of each class of the stock of a corporation or corporations (other than a corporation which has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by § 251(g)(7)(A) and (B) of this title), of which class there are outstanding shares that, absent this subsection, would be entitled to vote on such merger, is owned by an entity, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
DECLARE `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation` HAS
    `the corporation has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by § 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)`  IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 251(g)(7) (piece dg6)
    `there are outstanding shares of the class that, absent the subsection, would be entitled to vote on the merger`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of outstanding shares of the class`  IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those shares owned by the entity`  IS A NUMBER

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN c IS A `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a)(1) the class counts toward the 90 percent test` MEANS
        (NOT c's `the corporation has in its certificate of incorporation the provision required by § 251(g)(7)(A) and (B)`)
    AND c's `there are outstanding shares of the class that, absent the subsection, would be entitled to vote on the merger`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN c IS A `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`at least` (90%) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "the outstanding shares of the class")) (c's `the number of those shares owned by the entity`) (c's `the number of outstanding shares of the class`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN classes IS A LIST OF `s 267(a) Class of stock of a corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` MEANS
    BRANCH IF null (filter `s 267(a)(1) the class counts toward the 90 percent test` classes) THEN NOTHING
           IF any (GIVEN c YIELD `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` c EQUALS NOTHING) (filter `s 267(a)(1) the class counts toward the 90 percent test` classes) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (all (GIVEN c YIELD `s 267(a)(1) the entity owns at least 90 percent of the class` c EQUALS JUST TRUE) (filter `s 267(a)(1) the class counts toward the 90 percent test` classes))

-- (a)(2): "1 or more of such corporations is a corporation of this State".
-- src:1373 | (2) 1 or more of such corporations is a corporation of this State, unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such entity or such foreign corporations are formed or organized prohibit such merger, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the number of the corporations that are corporations of this State` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a)(2) 1 or more of the corporations is a corporation of this State` MEANS
    `the number of the corporations that are corporations of this State` AT LEAST 1

-- The power: where (1) and (2) hold, unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which the entity or the foreign corporations are formed or organized prohibit the merger, the entity may either
-- merge the corporation or corporations into itself and assume all of its or their obligations, or merge itself, or itself and 1 or more of them, into 1 of the other corporations. NOTHING when (1) cannot be decided.
-- src:1373 | unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such entity or such foreign corporations are formed or organized prohibit such merger, the entity having such stock ownership may either merge the corporation or corporations into itself and assume all of its or their obligations, or merge itself, or itself and 1 or more of such corporations, into 1 of the other corporations …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `1 or more of the corporations is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the jurisdiction under which the entity or a foreign corporation is formed or organized prohibit the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) the entity may merge under this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entity owns at least 90 percent of the outstanding shares of each class`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST owns THEN JUST (    owns
                              AND `1 or more of the corporations is a corporation of this State`
                              AND (NOT `the laws of the jurisdiction under which the entity or a foreign corporation is formed or organized prohibit the merger`))

DECLARE `s 267(a) How the entity merges` IS ONE OF
    `the entity merges the corporation or corporations into itself and assumes all of its or their obligations`
    `the entity merges itself, or itself and 1 or more of the corporations, into 1 of the other corporations`

-- Which party survives: if the entity merges the corporation or corporations into itself, the entity is the surviving constituent party; if it merges itself into one of the other
-- corporations, a corporation is.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN how IS A `s 267(a) How the entity merges`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) the entity is the surviving constituent party` how MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `the entity merges the corporation or corporations into itself and assumes all of its or their obligations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- By (a) authorizing the merger in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized, and (b) acknowledging and filing with the
-- Secretary of State, in accordance with section 103 (piece dg1), a certificate of ownership and merger certifying (i) that the merger was authorized in that way, the certificate executed in accordance with the
-- governing documents and the law of the entity's jurisdiction, and (ii) the type of entity of each constituent entity to the merger. If the entity does not own all the outstanding stock of all the corporations,
-- (A) the certificate states the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted by the surviving constituent party on surrender of
-- each share not owned by the entity, or the cancellation of some or all of them.
-- src:1373 | by (a) authorizing such merger in accordance with such entity’s governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which such entity is formed or organized and (b) acknowledging and filing with the Secretary of State, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of such ownership and merger certifying (i) that such merger was authorized in accordance with such entity’s governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which such entity is formed or organized, such certificate executed in accordance with such entity’s governing documents and in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction under which such entity is formed or organized and (ii) the type of entity of each constituent entity to the merger; provided, however, that in case the entity shall not own all the outstanding stock of all the corporations, parties to a merger as aforesaid, (A) the certificate of ownership and merger shall state the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property, or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted by the surviving constituent party upon surrender of each share of the corporation or corporations not owned by the entity, or the cancellation of some or all of such shares and …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
