    `s 267(a)(b)(i) the certificate certifies that the merger was authorized in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which the entity is formed or organized`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 267(a)(b)(ii) the certificate certifies the type of entity of each constituent entity to the merger`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 267(a)(A) the certificate states the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted by the surviving constituent party upon surrender of each share not owned by the entity, or the cancellation of some or all of those shares`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the entity authorized the merger in accordance with its governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of ownership and merger was acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
      `the certificate was executed in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      certifications IS A `s 267(a) Certifications in the certificate of ownership and merger`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) the merger has been authorized and the certificate of ownership and merger filed as the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the entity authorized the merger in accordance with its governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized`
    AND `the certificate of ownership and merger was acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103`
    AND `the certificate was executed in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which it is formed or organized`
    AND certifications's `s 267(a)(b)(i) the certificate certifies that the merger was authorized in accordance with the entity's governing documents and the laws of the jurisdiction under which the entity is formed or organized`
    AND certifications's `s 267(a)(b)(ii) the certificate certifies the type of entity of each constituent entity to the merger`
    -- the proviso, (A): "in case the entity shall not own all the outstanding stock of all the corporations"
    AND (   `the entity owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations party to the merger`
         OR certifications's `s 267(a)(A) the certificate states the terms and conditions of the merger, including the securities, cash, property or rights to be issued, paid, delivered or granted by the surviving constituent party upon surrender of each share not owned by the entity, or the cancellation of some or all of those shares`)

-- The proviso, (B): where the entity does not own all the outstanding stock of all the corporations, the terms and conditions "may not result in a holder of stock in a corporation becoming a general
-- partner in a surviving entity that is a partnership (other than a limited liability partnership or a limited liability limited partnership)". The stockholder's side: an immunity from being made a general partner.
-- src:1373 | (B) such terms and conditions of the merger may not result in a holder of stock in a corporation becoming a general partner in a surviving entity that is a partnership (other than a limited liability partnership or a limited liability limited partnership). …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the entity owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions of the merger result in a holder of stock in a corporation becoming a general partner in the surviving entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of the surviving entity` IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a)(B) the terms and conditions of the merger are permitted` MEANS
    -- "a partnership (other than a limited liability partnership or a limited liability limited partnership)" is a general partnership or a limited partnership
    IF   (NOT `the entity owns all the outstanding stock of all the corporations party to the merger`)
     AND `the terms and conditions of the merger result in a holder of stock in a corporation becoming a general partner in the surviving entity`
     AND (CONSIDER `the kind of the surviving entity`
          WHEN `a general partnership` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a limited partnership` THEN TRUE
          OTHERWISE FALSE)
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE TRUE

-- The terms of the merger may depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate of ownership and merger, provided that the manner in which the facts operate on the terms is clearly and expressly set forth
-- in the certificate. (The next sentence, on what "facts" includes, is inert: keel instruction 15.)
-- src:1373 | Any of the terms of the merger may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the certificate of ownership and merger, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the merger is clearly and expressly set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the term depends on facts ascertainable outside the certificate of ownership and merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which those facts operate on the term is clearly and expressly set forth in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) the term may depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` MEANS
        (NOT `the term depends on facts ascertainable outside the certificate of ownership and merger`)
    OR  `the manner in which those facts operate on the term is clearly and expressly set forth in the certificate`

-- The sentence after it: "The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the entity."
-- "Includes, but is not limited to" makes the list of facts open; it does not make everything a fact. An event, and a determination or action by any person or body
-- (including the entity), are facts; for anything else the text does not say, so the rule answers NOTHING (fork F26).
-- src:1373 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the entity. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
DECLARE `s 267(a) Kind of fact` IS ONE OF
    `the occurrence of an event under s 267(a)`
    `a determination by any person or body, including the entity, under s 267(a)`
    `an action by any person or body, including the entity, under s 267(a)`
    `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 267(a)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 267(a) Kind of fact`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) the kind of fact is within the term facts` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action under s 267(a)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- If the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State: (1) section 252(d) (piece dg6) also applies to a merger under this section, and where the
-- surviving constituent party is the entity "corporation" in section 252(d) is deemed to include an entity as defined here; (2) the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party to
-- provide the agreement, and take the actions, section 252(d) requires.
-- src:1373 | If the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State, (1) § 252(d) of this title shall also apply to a merger under this section; if the surviving constituent party is the entity, the word “corporation” where applicable, as used in § 252(d) of this title, shall be deemed to include an entity as defined herein; and (2) the terms and conditions of the merger shall obligate the surviving constituent party to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by § 252(d) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) section 252(d) also applies to the merger` MEANS
    `the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surviving constituent party is the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) the word corporation in section 252(d) is deemed to include the entity` MEANS
        `the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`
    AND `the surviving constituent party is the entity`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(a) (src:1373)
GIVEN `the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by § 252(d)` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 252(d) (piece dg6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(a) the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party as section 252(d) requires` MEANS
        (NOT `the surviving constituent party is an entity formed or organized under the laws of a jurisdiction other than this State`)
    OR  `the terms and conditions of the merger obligate the surviving constituent party to provide the agreement, and take the actions, required by § 252(d)`

§ `s 267(b) Provisions applied by reference; section 262 does not apply`

-- Sections 259, 261 and 328 apply, insofar as applicable, to a merger under the section; sections 260 and 251(e) apply to a merger in which the surviving constituent party is a corporation of this State.
-- References to "agreement of merger" in 251(e) mean the terms and conditions in the certificate of ownership and merger; references to "corporation" in 259-261 and 328 include the entity, as applicable.
-- src:1374 | (b) Sections 259, 261, and 328 of this title shall, insofar as they are applicable, apply to a merger under this section, and §§ 260 and 251(e) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section in which the surviving constituent party is a corporation of this State. For purposes of this subsection, references to “agreement of merger” in § 251(e) of this title shall mean the terms and conditions of the merger set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger, and references to “corporation” in §§ 259-261 of this title, and § 328 of this title shall be deemed to include the entity, as applicable. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b) (src:1374)
DECLARE `s 267(b) Provision applied by reference` IS ONE OF
    `s 259 as applied by s 267(b)`
    `s 261 as applied by s 267(b)`
    `s 328 as applied by s 267(b)`
    `s 260 as applied by s 267(b)`
    `s 251(e) as applied by s 267(b)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b) (src:1374)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 267(b) Provision applied by reference`
      `the provision is applicable to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surviving constituent party is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(b) the provision applies to the merger` MEANS
        `the provision is applicable to the merger`
    AND (CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `s 260 as applied by s 267(b)` THEN `the surviving constituent party is a corporation of this State`
         WHEN `s 251(e) as applied by s 267(b)` THEN `the surviving constituent party is a corporation of this State`
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- For purposes of the subsection, references to "agreement of merger" in section 251(e) mean the terms and conditions of the merger set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger,
-- and references to "corporation" in sections 259 to 261 and 328 are deemed to include the entity, as applicable. A construction rule for the provisions applied by reference.
-- src:1374 | For purposes of this subsection, references to “agreement of merger” in § 251(e) of this title shall mean the terms and conditions of the merger set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger, and references to “corporation” in §§ 259-261 of this title, and § 328 of this title shall be deemed to include the entity, as applicable. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b) (src:1374)
DECLARE `s 267(b) Reference in a provision applied by s 267(b)` IS ONE OF
    `the words agreement of merger in s 251(e)`
    `the word corporation in ss 259 to 261`
    `the word corporation in s 328`

DECLARE `s 267(b) How a reference is read` IS ONE OF
    `the terms and conditions of the merger set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger`
    `a corporation or, as applicable, the entity`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b) (src:1374)
GIVEN reference IS A `s 267(b) Reference in a provision applied by s 267(b)`
GIVETH A `s 267(b) How a reference is read`
`s 267(b) the way the reference is read` reference MEANS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `the words agreement of merger in s 251(e)` THEN `the terms and conditions of the merger set forth in the certificate of ownership and merger`
    WHEN `the word corporation in ss 259 to 261` THEN `a corporation or, as applicable, the entity`
    WHEN `the word corporation in s 328` THEN `a corporation or, as applicable, the entity`

-- "Section 262 of this title shall not apply to any merger effected under this section, except as provided in subsection (c)": it applies exactly as (c) provides.
-- src:1374 | Section 262 of this title shall not apply to any merger effected under this section, except as provided in subsection (c) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(b) (src:1374)
GIVEN `all of the stock of the Delaware corporation party to the merger was owned by the entity immediately prior to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(b) section 262 applies to the merger` MEANS
    `s 267(c) the stockholders of the Delaware corporation have appraisal rights as set forth in section 262` `all of the stock of the Delaware corporation party to the merger was owned by the entity immediately prior to the merger`

§ `s 267(c) Appraisal rights where the entity does not own all the stock`

-- "In the event all of the stock of a Delaware corporation party to a merger effected under this section is not owned by the entity immediately prior to the merger, the stockholders of such Delaware corporation
-- party to the merger shall have appraisal rights as set forth in § 262": read as "if not all of the stock is owned by the entity" (fork F17). Whether a given stockholder meets section 262's own conditions
-- (a demand, a record holding and the rest) is for piece dg7; this rule gives the right that section 267 opens.
-- src:1375 | (c) In the event all of the stock of a Delaware corporation party to a merger effected under this section is not owned by the entity immediately prior to the merger, the stockholders of such Delaware corporation party to the merger shall have appraisal rights as set forth in § 262 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 267(c) (src:1375)
GIVEN `all of the stock of the Delaware corporation party to the merger was owned by the entity immediately prior to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 267(c) the stockholders of the Delaware corporation have appraisal rights as set forth in section 262` MEANS
    NOT `all of the stock of the Delaware corporation party to the merger was owned by the entity immediately prior to the merger`
